{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwTCce3EFYoaXSo5aquv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. Its status was still \"pending\" right after creation, so it hasn't run yet. I didn't open the dashboard, so I haven't seen how the panels render.\n\n**What the data holds:** `kibana_sample_data_logs` has one document per web request. Useful fields include `timestamp`, `response` (status code, stored as text with a `.keyword` subfield), `bytes`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest`, `clientip`, `extension`, `machine.os` and `url`. A count by response code shows 12,832 requests with 200, 801 with 404 and 441 with 503. The only 5xx code in the data is 503.\n\n**Dashboard \"EFF-1424cba4 Web logs overview\"** has five panels:\n- Total requests (metric)\n- Requests over time (area chart)\n- Responses by status code (pie chart)\n- Total bytes over time (line chart)\n- Top 10 source countries (bar chart)\n\nIt is at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-1424cba4-web-logs-overview-8402dd3161ef.\n\n**Rule \"EFF-1424cba4 5xx spike\"** (id `9bcc62e7-57ba-40a8-a5cf-7bf0a3d7ba94`):\n- It is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute.\n- It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` where `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]`, over a 5-minute window.\n- It fires when that count is above 10.\n- It has no actions attached, so a firing only shows up in Kibana, not as a notification.\n- Sample-data timestamps are fixed when the data is loaded and don't keep advancing. The rule may therefore find nothing in a live 5-minute window until the data is refreshed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":602,"cache_read_input_tokens":20746,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":602},"output_tokens":613,"service_tier":"